1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,140
 I'm Susan Craig. I live in NDG in the Loyola District. I've lived here about 50 years.

2
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:15,560
 And I just want to thank all the council for your openness to listen to both sides of all the

3
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:22,620
 discussions. I think there's a lot of angst over the Terrebonne bike path and some other things.

4
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:28,220
 And I've just noticed that you're really good at listening and trying to come to some solution

5
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:33,760
 that's equitable for all the players. And I really appreciate that. I hope we can build

6
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:39,720
 a community that picks up that spirit. And I know people have a lot of angst about the

7
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:44,920
 closures, but maybe we could work together for the future, for the other players too.

8
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,320
 So thank you very much.

9
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:50,500
 Thank you, Ms. Craig.

10
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:54,040
 Prochaine question de Lee Adams.

11
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:56,420
 Lee?

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:57,180
 Pardon?

13
00:00:58,220 --> 00:00:59,580
 No.

14
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,240
 Catherine Lund.

15
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:19,500
 Hi. I mean, obviously there's a lot of questions about the Terrebonne bike path. So I'm sure

16
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:26,220
 everybody is heartily sick of hearing about it, but here we go, one more. So clearly from

17
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:30,680
 your responses to the people that have come up earlier, you've already made up your mind

18
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:34,740
 and you've already decided how you're going to vote tonight. I think that's kind of a shame

19
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:40,360
 because this is the first time you are really hearing from the population how they feel about

20
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:44,440
 this. And I know you've done door to door during your political campaigns, but that is

21
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:52,440
 not the same thing as consulting during normal times when people are no longer in a vote.

22
00:01:52,440 --> 00:02:00,660
 So I also noticed that the counselors from Anselm Morial, you refused the paper copy of the 1,500 signatures

23
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:07,800
 or thereabouts that, well, okay. Okay. Well, you originally refused it when it was handed to you

24
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:15,240
 by a member of the cycling association. And I just want to let you know what is in that. Okay. That is 12 days of citizens going,

25
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:22,180
 speaking to people on the street in front of schools, work that you probably should have been doing and asking

26
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:27,480
 them how they felt about the table and bike path, about the changes that you were about to bring.

27
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:34,700
 And we showed them our petition, our little paper, the picture. And we asked them, you know, do you know what's going on?

28
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:39,700
 Do you know how it's going to change? And the reality is that most people were not aware that you were about to make these changes.

29
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:48,920
 And so for you to be already voting on this, when people clearly don't know what it is that you were about to do, I think it's very unfair.

30
00:02:48,920 --> 00:03:00,020
 And so that, again, that's almost 1,500 people in the petition. And in Cote de Nege and DG alone, there's 1,128 people.

31
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:09,020
 So, and within one block of the tailbone bike path, there was 464 people. Now, that's not everybody. It's only 12 days.

32
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:14,980
 We were going door, we weren't doing the door-to-door. We were just standing outside of schools and asking people to sign online.

33
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:26,200
 So I think if you can see that almost 1,500 people are against your changes in just 12 days of asking them their opinions, that maybe you've made up your mind just a little too soon.

34
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:35,660
 Okay. So before you vote on motion 30-02, I would like you to reconsider. So is the path perfect? No.

35
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:39,900
 Are there local residents that don't like it? Yeah, many of them are here tonight.

36
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:47,200
 But does it make our kids and our bikers safer? Definitely. And can it save lives? Yes.

37
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:51,920
 And that's not a theoretical thing. I have been hit by a car as a pedestrian.

38
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:59,100
 My husband has been hit by a car as a biker. He ended up with cracked ribs, concussion, scars all over.

39
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:08,900
 My stepson was hit by a car on a bike on Terrebonne right in front of Wellington about five or six years ago.

40
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:12,540
 His bike was totaled. He was bruised all over, but he is still walking.

41
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:20,200
 So those that think that that's a really safe street because it's really cute and it's got trees and it seems slow, it's still not necessarily safe.

42
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:27,280
 And when you propose to take away that path, well, it's people like my stepson that might end up in a wheelchair for that change.

43
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:41,700
 So what I'd like to ask you, first of all, is before you vote on it, have you communicated to the community what it is that you are really planning to do and what will be coming back in the spring?

44
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:47,040
 So, one, where is the detailed layout of what you're going to change?

45
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:55,440
 So there are areas like in front of St. Monica's and in front of the, like where the road changes at Cavendish that are not easy to change.

46
00:04:55,780 --> 00:05:09,040
 And when you say you're only taking it off on one side, I want you to think about you're biking along at Cavendish, you hit the red light, now you have to kitty corner to the other side because the traffic changes direction there and you're going to have to be biking on the other side.

47
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:13,680
 Do I want a child crossing diagonally on Cavendish and Talban?

48
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:14,520
 Obviously not.

49
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:21,860
 So until we actually see your plan, I don't think anybody here can be sure that it is a safe one.

50
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:25,600
 Also, thank you.

51
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:33,540
 And then my second question is, what kind of path will you be bringing back in the spring?

52
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:36,520
 Because you keep talking about a temporary change.

53
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:40,440
 But nobody really believes that, okay?

54
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:50,400
 We all know that once you've come and you've scrubbed off all of the yellow lines, you've taken out the bollards, and you've put it only on one side, and you've put in a new paint line so the cars can park and the signs.

55
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,740
 When it comes to spring, you're not going to undo all of that.

56
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,940
 You're going to put something else in its place.

57
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:57,680
 What is that something else?

58
00:05:57,960 --> 00:06:03,020
 And before you vote, you should be sharing that information with all of us.

59
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:05,240
 So where is that information, please?

60
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:14,080
 I find it very interesting that you're assuming immediately that what we're saying is incorrect because clearly you don't trust us.

61
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:23,680
 And I totally understand why you would think that we're not trustable because you've clearly positioned yourself on our administration.

62
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:41,000
 I just want to share that in the previous mandate, I was elected, and the multiple times residents that were not necessarily in favor of the proposed bike path, petitions were deposed with over 1,500 signatures as well.

63
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:47,300
 And those petitions were never considered by the previous administration with regards to the impact that it had on those residents.

64
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:50,840
 We're an administration that is looking at both sides.

65
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:59,460
 And I understand, listen, what happened to your stepson, what happened to you, I'm sorry, that's not something that we want in our city.

66
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:01,360
 That's not something that we want in our borough.

67
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:20,440
 But, again, in a spirit of transparency in September, even if there was nothing clear to propose yet or to share, we wanted to alert the residents with regards to the one question that was clearly constantly asked to us with regards to what are you going to do with the Taqban bike path.

68
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:26,140
 The first council that we had, it was an extraordinary council after we were elected in the month of November.

69
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:29,760
 The first question that we had received is what are you going to do with the bike path?

70
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:36,400
 You've gone door knocking, you heard us, Sunny and myself, we sat in the council in the opposition in the previous mandate.

71
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:42,740
 And all we did was listen to every single council meeting that somebody raised both perspectives.

72
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:51,740
 And I think that we are in this position today with a lot of discontent because the previous administration didn't take the time to listen to both perspectives.

73
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:57,980
 And I understand that you're going to react that way, but, I mean, everybody has a different perspective in this room,

74
00:07:57,980 --> 00:08:03,460
 whether it's for keeping the bike path on both sides or completely removing it once again.

75
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:15,600
 We're trying to find a middle ground that allows for the infrastructure to stay in place and to eventually add more infrastructure that is clearly needed in the borough of Kodanej and DG.

76
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:21,760
 Again, the proposition is to only remove one side of the bike path for the four months.

77
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:23,720
 And then after that, it comes back.

78
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:27,460
 And so the both sides will be usable for the rest of the season.

79
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:38,320
 Again, we're waiting for the film to have it ready for deployment in December.

80
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:40,940
 We don't have that documentation yet.

81
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:48,460
 But we, again, in the spirit of transparency and alerting and communicating with our residents,

82
00:08:48,660 --> 00:08:52,320
 we're sharing this with you because we want to hear from everybody.

83
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:59,840
 We want to understand the impact that it will have, and we want to make sure that it responds to the needs of all residents in the borough,

84
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:07,780
 including those that have lived over 35 years on Tarbonne, that have reduced mobility,

85
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:14,760
 that don't necessarily have the capacity to walk a few blocks and that need the parking right in front of their home.

86
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:17,140
 There are needs in all of that.

87
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:18,700
 We are an aging population.

88
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:22,460
 More than 30% of our population is at reduced mobility.

89
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:29,320
 And we have to be able to consider the needs of all our residents, from young children to our senior population.

90
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:36,500
 There are the HLMs on Tarbonne that clearly had some issues as well with the mise en place of the piece of Tarbonne.

91
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:44,460
 So everybody coming to this council meeting has a very valid perspective and a very valid experience.

92
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:48,860
 In no way are we trying to invalidate all of those experiences.

93
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:56,400
 What we're trying to do as an administration is find, again, a pathway that is able to respond to the needs of our residents

94
00:09:56,400 --> 00:10:03,180
 in a way that ensures that we can go forward in the future with additional infrastructure.

95
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:11,480
 Okay, so you did answer my first question, which is where are the details so that we, the public, that you say are consulting?

96
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:18,240
 I literally just said that our colleagues are working on it with the external firm, and as soon as we have them, they will become public.

97
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:20,160
 But you're voting before that?

98
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:25,280
 What we're voting on is to transfer, which is exactly what the previous administration did.

99
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:34,940
 Because it's an agglomeration jurisdiction, you have to request from municipal council the ability to put in place the change.

100
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:37,300
 There's a three vote that we're doing.

101
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:39,280
 We're sending it to municipal council.

102
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:40,820
 It's going to municipal council.

103
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:41,640
 It's going to be voted.

104
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:48,400
 And once they allow us that jurisdiction to put in place the change that we need in our borough, we're going to be able to vote it again in December.

105
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:54,640
 So for multiple times, people are going to be able to come to council and share their perspective and ask us questions.

106
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:55,800
 We respond to them.

107
00:10:55,900 --> 00:11:01,340
 But we've never hidden our intention, and we've always answered the questions of our residents.

108
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:02,100
 Okay.

109
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:11,020
 Well, then I'd like to mention that we have seen your mandate letter to Mr. Teodorescu, which asks him to change the bike path for the entire year.

110
00:11:11,020 --> 00:11:16,240
 Mr. Teodorescu is a councillor, so I don't know if your information is correct.

111
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:21,880
 But at the same time, you've answered, I mean, you've gotten your chance to ask your two questions.

112
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:23,940
 And so I thank you for your presence tonight.

113
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:24,920
 Well, don't I get three questions?

114
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:25,980
 No, you don't.

115
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:26,500
 It's two questions.

116
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:29,880
 So you can say something that in the documents that you've shared with us seems to be true?

117
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:33,260
 Every single resident that has shown up to our council meeting has asked two questions.

118
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:37,440
 We've had a few back and forths that are technically not permitted in the Régieng town.

119
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,520
 So again, thank you for coming to council.

120
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:41,700
 We're going to pass on to another person.

121
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:51,320
 Le temps est écoulé, oui, pour la période de questions.

122
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:52,900
 Parfait.

123
00:11:54,260 --> 00:11:55,000
 Five minutes a break.

124
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:56,100
 Merci beaucoup.

125
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:06,040
 There's other questions as well about Tara Vaughn, myself and Stephen Jass.

126
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:06,560
 Okay.

127
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:07,280
 Thank you.

128
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:13,340
 There were two questions in person.

129
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:16,260
 We're going to do the extension of 15 minutes, then we're going to leave them.

130
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:17,780
 Pardon?

131
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:19,020
 In the present.

132
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,000
 There were two questions.

